Rule 2 (tuple of axes elements must be within non-negative dimension bounds)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (list of axes length should not exceed tensor rank and elements must be valid indices)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor should have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (axes sequence as tuple or list length cannot exceed tensor dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int) ⊎ list(int)} |= v_2.len > 0 ∧ v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)
